							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1066.msg10636#msg10636"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1066.msg10636#msg10636">Re: What class will you play in EQ2?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #11 on:</b> August 30, 2004, 11:28:35 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Because EQ2 &quot;looks better&quot; is why, and we all know that graphics &gt; gameplay&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/bullshit.gif" alt="Bull Shit!" border="0" /><br /><br />Really, other than what Sony SAYS about their game, and their pretty screenshots (anyone remember SWG?), very little is known about EQ2.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
